.TH EDSPRITE 1
.SH NAME
edsprite \- outline a sprite by reading it back
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/edsprite
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I EdSprite
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/EdSprite.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Twelve sprites given a black outline one pixel wide, by the simplest
method there is: draw each into a buffer one pixel larger all round, walk
every transparent pixel, and blacken it if any of its eight neighbours is
neither transparent, nor black, nor off the edge.  No edge detection and
no geometry \- it reads back the pixels it has just drawn.
.PP
The original prints the outlined sprites to the command line so they can
be cut and pasted into source; here they are drawn in a row, since a
sprite in this tree is a file rather than a run of characters in a
document.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/edsprite.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
